On time:

You asked whether time is really a dimension.

In modern physics, spacetime is modeled as a four-dimensional manifold with one temporal dimension and three spatial dimensions. That mathematical model has been extraordinarily successful at explaining experiments.

However, there are active research questions about whether time is fundamental or emergent. Some approaches to quantum gravity explore the possibility that spacetime itself—including time—emerges from deeper structures. Those remain areas of ongoing research rather than established fact.

