I particularly liked your closing metaphor:

Life isn’t a microscopic slice of a cell. It’s hydrated and lives in many unique ways.

As an engineering analogy, I’d translate it into:

Static representations are slices through dynamic systems.

A blueprint isn’t the building.

A genome isn’t the organism.

Source code isn’t the running program.

A repository isn’t the practice.

Each is a representation of something that unfolds over time through interaction.

That suggests another Pantheon distinction:

